.\" Manpage for sxalert

.TH man 1 "13 Oct 2026" "1.0" "sxalert manual page"
.SH NAME
sxalert \- Simple X Alert

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sxalert
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR color ]
.RB [ \-g
.IR color ]
.RB [ \-r
.IR color ]
.RB [ \-b
.IR width ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR duration ]
.RI [ line " ...]"
.br
.B sxalert \-v
.br
.B sxalert \-h

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sxalert
displays text notifications for X. It accepts standard input,
command-line arguments, or both, appending the latter to the former.
Mouse interactions produce distinct exit statuses, allowing sxalert
to be used in shell scripts. It allows for runtime visual
customizability through command-line arguments.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B -s
Read from stdin. Command line arguments will be appended.

.TP
.BI "-t " color
Set the text color in hexadecimal. Six consecutive digits without prefix.

.TP
.BI "-g " color
Set the background color.

.TP
.BI "-r " color
Set the border color.

.TP
.BI "-b " width
Set the border width in pixels.

.TP
.BI "-d " duration
Set the duration in milliseconds. Will run indefinitely for values less than, or equal to, zero.

.TP
.B -h
Print help panel & exit.

.TP
.B -v
Print version & exit.

.SH EXIT CODES

.TP
.B 0
Left click on the notification window.

.TP
.B 1
Midde click on the notification window.

.TP
.B 2
Right click on the notification window.

.TP
.B 3
Time out.

.SH EXAMPLES

Display a simple notification:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sxalert "Updates available"
.fi
.RE

Display a notification with red text, black background, no border:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sxalert -t 0xff0000 -g 0x000000 -b 0 "Updates available"
.fi
.RE

These options override the defaults in config.h.
.PP

Confirmation dialoge with a right click, dismissed otherwise:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sxalert "Proceed with backup?" && backup.sh
.fi
.RE

Launch neomutt in st when the notification is accepted; otherwise display "Ignored":
.PP
.RS
.nf
sxalert "New mail!" && nohup st -e neomutt || sxalert "Ignored"
.fi
.RE

Display a preformatted text file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sxalert -s < banner.txt
.fi
.RE

Display stdin and append a timestamp:
.PP
.RS
.nf
make test | tail | sxalert -s "$(date)"
.fi
.RE

